1 The morning began quietly
2 with fog over the river
3 and a heron standing still
4 at the edge of the reeds

5 A boat drifted past slowly
6 its engine barely a whisper
7 while gulls circled overhead
8 calling to one another
9 The town was waking up
10 shutters rattled open one by one
11 a baker carried trays of bread
12 into the cold bright street
13 Children ran toward the school
14 bags bouncing on their backs
15 and a dog chased after them
16 barking at nothing in particular
17 By noon the fog had lifted
18 revealing hills to the north
19 green and gold in the sunlight
20 dotted with sheep and stone walls
21 The afternoon passed lazily
22 in the market square
23 where traders called out prices
24 and tourists took photographs
25 Evening brought a cool breeze
26 lamps flickered on along the quay
27 the heron returned to the reeds
28 and the river turned to silver
29 Night settled over everything
30 The End
